WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:13.280
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.920
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.980
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.390
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:27.500
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.640
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:37.200
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:41.390
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.460
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.550
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:58.310
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.590
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:05.520
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:12.970
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:25.280
Takara Fansubs

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:34.770
<i>Rossi's mother had come to visit for the first time in ages.</i>

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:40.020
<i>Although she nagged a little, the kindly grandmother...</i>

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:45.460
<i>...left Angeletta and Romeo with a warm memory in their hearts.</i>

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:50.920
Episode 20:

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:50.920
Grampa Theo's Puppet Show

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.870
The rain stopped.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.160
Good morning.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.490
The smell of autumn!

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.020
Each day the wind grows a little colder.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.850
What a tender fragrance.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:35.120
<i>Angeletta has been looking out of this window for years now.</i>

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:41.980
<i>None of the events in Bolgo Alley below escaped her knowledge.</i>

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.580
The morning sun has risen past the treetops,

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.350
...so Mr. Zebetto should be leaving soon.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.460
Good morning, Angeletta!
- Good Morning!

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.100
...See?

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.080
See you later!

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.290
He's swaying his shoulders - something good has happened.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.840
He always does that when he's happy.

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:14.160
Oh no... Angeletta, it's Mrs. Madela's place!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.280
If we don't do something, they'll tear the house down.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.400
Wait one moment.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:23.810
That bracelet was a memento of my mother. How could you sell it?

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:26.720
You're wrong, the only thing I sold was that pot.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:30.820
No, you sold my precious bracelet, too!

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:34.520
Bracelet? It was Cleopatra.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:35.850
Cleopatra?

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.990
It must have been her.
Cleopatra loves shiny things.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:43.690
Mrs. Madera.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:45.850
Good mo...

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:51.580
I'm telling the truth!
I didn't sell your bracelet!

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:55.420
Don't give me that story!
- Angeletta says... the thief!...

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.530
IS CLEOPATRA!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.520
Cleopatra?

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.780
Over there.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.780
Cleopatra!

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.860
Cleopatra!

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:21.410
If you said that at the beginning, I wouldn't have blamed you.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:29.740
Thanks, Angeletta!

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:33.600
How many times has Angeletta put a stop to one of our arguments?

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:36.990
Angeletta's our guardian angel.

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.260
I'll bring you a pie later on, okay?

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.590
Romeo, can I ask one more favor of you?

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:48.080
Eh?

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.810
Across the way, at Grampa Theo's place.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.450
Oh, you mean the old puppet master who moved in recently?

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.710
It's little Nana's birthday over there.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:01.100
Yes? Come in.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.550
Hello there.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:04.830
Welcome.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.510
Little Nana... Happy Birthday!

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.020
Here you are. A present from Angeletta.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:15.190
Oh, from Angeletta?
- How pretty!

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.770
Why, Nana, you look like the princess of the flowers!

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.730
Thank you... umm...

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:24.800
Romeo.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.200
Right, Romeo.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.900
I knew from the day I moved in...

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:35.950
...that Angeletta was spreading around happiness from that window.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.670
Happiness?

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:41.950
Angeletta is happy whenever she sees somebody else that's happy.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:43.690
Hey there.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:57.840
<i>All right! I'll help Angeletta spread around happiness!</i>

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.790
Hmm? Did you say something?

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.500
I said Angeletta is like an angel!

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.310
Everybody says so, too.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:07.140
Right, boss?

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.660
Well - didn't you know?
She really IS an angel.

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.070
An angel?

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:18.510
Long, long ago, she flew onto my pillow with a tiny pair of wings.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:24.800
What can I say - God finally noticed what a honest man I am.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.180
You can talk! You little teapot, short and stout.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:31.780
And that I'm a lady-killer, too, on top of honest.

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:37.380
The truth is, ten years ago...

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.670
Ten years ago?

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:43.020
When this guy was a regular visitor at a certain count's house...

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.320
Ow-ow...

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.810
You idiot! What are you saying?

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:51.600
Is it still a secret that Angeletta isn't really your child, but...?

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:52.810
Shh.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.510
What are you looking at? Go on, get to work!

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:58.760
Y-Yes.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.020
Something smells fishy.
- Yeah.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:09.520
And Little Red Riding Hood opened the bed's curtain.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:13.750
"What big ears you have, Grandma."

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:18.250
"The better to hear you with, my dear."

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:22.880
"What a big mouth you have, Grandma."

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.430
"Yes, my dear..."

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.560
"The better to eat you with!"

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:29.880
CHOMP!

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.170
Well, that's all for today.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:46.570
Angeletta! Don't you think so too? Isn't Grampa great?

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.830
You know, Grampa can talk to the moon!

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.660
To the moon?
- Yeah!

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.650
Last night the moon and I sang a lullaby...

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.880
...to little Nana the prankster here.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:01.360
I love you, Grampa!
- Yes, yes.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:02.790
Grampa!

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.900
Suppose Angeletta and I...

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:08.720
...were to take you to the land of the stars tonight?

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.630
I'm so happy!

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:15.910
Oh, it's raining again.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:20.100
Umm, did you know that it doesn't rain in heaven?

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.530
Because Mom and Dad live there!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:29.790
Grampa said that Dad lives in heaven...

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:34.270
...so even though I can't see him, I don't need to be sad.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:35.920
Right, Grampa?

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:39.250
Uh... Yes...
That's right.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:47.740
<i>Some time earlier, Angeletta had become aware...</i>

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:52.280
<i>...that Grampa Theo was hiding a painful secret.</i>

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:12.950
I'm sorry, Nana.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:17.540
Your Grampa is a liar.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.300
Angeletta!

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.900
Should you be coming out here like this?

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:30.190
This way it's warm.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:34.000
It was said in an old story...

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.750
...that a grampa has the kindly smell of tobacco.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:42.400
That odor of tobacco about you brings memories back to me.

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:46.300
You're trying to cheer me up.

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:48.530
What a kindhearted child.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:54.920
Those magic ears of yours hear every one of my sorrows, Angeletta.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.540
Grampa Theo...

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:01.130
Will you listen to my story?

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.630
It isn't a fairy-tale or a fantasy.

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:09.800
Just a slightly bitter, real life story.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:18.330
Long ago, the three of us - Nana, Nana's father Leon, and I...

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:22.870
We travelled around the country putting on puppet shows.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.550
I greatly enjoyed our travels.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.670
But Leon... my son... was different.

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:35.340
Ever since childhood, he had wanted to become a doctor.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.210
He was completely uninterested in the puppet show.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:42.550
Leon! When will you give up this foolishness?

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:45.060
Be a good son, and take over the puppet show.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.410
What's so bad about that?

00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:51.870
Father, I'm serious about becoming a doctor.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.730
Please, let me study.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.520
It was right about that time that Nana got very sick.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.290
Neither of us could do anything to help her.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:04.640
Thankfully, Nana was spared.

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:08.050
But because of that, Leon just became more stubborn.

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:10.390
I want to become a doctor!

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:13.670
Then I can help the children going through what Nana went through.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:18.610
What good could you do? You who'd leave Nana behind!

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:24.320
Fine, get out. And don't ever let me see your face again.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:29.520
The next day, Leon was nowhere to be seen.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:38.690
I was a fool. Nana, Leon and I - we all loved each other.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.580
Where's Leon now?

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:47.130
Some time ago, I heard a rumor that he'd been seen in this town.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:48.920
That's why we came here.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:55.330
But it's too late, no matter how much I may regret it now.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:02.580
Life is sad, Angeletta.

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:19.690
What's wrong, Angeletta?

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:21.780
Romeo, I've got a favor to ask.

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:22.580
Eh?

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:27.160
So... Nana's father is here in Milan?

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:30.220
It's only a rumor, and it might not even be true.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:34.900
But I want to believe in miracles.

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:40.050
Because Grampa Theo's such a kind person, after all.

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:45.260
So you want to reunite Leon with Nana and Grampa Theo?

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:48.670
All right, then!

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:52.660
Leave it to me, Angeletta.
I'll find him for sure.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:00.750
The man's name is Leon, and he has chestnut hair and blue eyes.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:03.550
Chestnut hair... Blue eyes...

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.090
What other clues are there?

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.000
That's it.

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:10.340
That's ridiculous.
- How are we supposed to find him?

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:15.100
You've got to be joking, Romeo.
You're not even sure he's IN Milan.

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:16.510
Yeah...

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:20.660
Listen! The more challenging it is,

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:22.110
...the more courage it'll give you.

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:24.820
Isn't that what the Black Brothers are all about?

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:26.940
The more challenging it is...?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:30.490
If we divide up the work, we should be able to comb the entire city.

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:33.530
After all, can't we get into every house?

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:35.450
Chimney cleaning!

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:39.040
I get it! We'll climb up the chimneys all over Milan!

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:42.700
Right - let's find Leon together.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:43.910
Right!

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.280
His name is Leon.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:52.350
Chestnut colored hair...

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:54.030
Blue eyes...

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.240
Sorry.

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:57.090
About thirty years old...

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:58.880
I don't know him.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.700
Don't you have any further description?

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:04.010
<i>Please, God...</i>

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.650
<i>...just for Grampa Theo and little Nana...</i>

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.810
<i>...please, give us a miracle...</i>

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:17.020
Come near! See the pirate and the mermaid princess!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:20.720
Theo's thrilling puppet show is about to begin!

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:22.060
About to begin!

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:22.880
That's correct.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.980
His name is Leon.
Chestnut-color hair.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:27.880
Chestnut-color, okay, whatever.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:28.980
Romeo!

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:30.840
How did it go?

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:32.360
Nothing over by the park.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:35.730
Hey - Grampa Theo!

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.940
We're going to find Leon for you!

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:41.500
Just wait 'n see.

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:42.410
Be waiting, okay?

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:43.110
Okay.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.930
We'll come watch your puppet show next time around!

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.840
Bye-bye!

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.660
Romeo... Thank you.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.110
Do you know a person named Leon?

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:01.830
Leon? Never heard of him.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:08.260
We're looking for a man named Leon.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:10.330
Good ol' Leon, you say?

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.540
What cuties!

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:14.650
Stop in for a belt?

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.720
Listen, boss! I'm trying to ask if you know a guy named Leon...

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:23.050
I told you, no! Now go do your work!

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.230
How'd it go, Romeo?

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:26.980
Nothing at all!

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:54.370
<i>All too quickly, ten days passed by without turning up a single clue.</i>

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:57.500
You've all looked from there to over here for me.

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:00.680
Next we'll check the other side of the great cathedral.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.420
And then...

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:07.530
You never get tired, do you, Romeo?

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:09.890
Get tired? How could I?

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:13.350
I'm DETERMINED to help Angeletta.

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:16.610
Angeletta wants to make everybody happy!

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:18.880
But she can't go outside, you know, so...

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:23.290
So I do the flying around for her... like those birds.

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:34.200
Come to think of it, those birds nested in Prof. Casera's chimney.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:36.870
That's it! A doctor!

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:37.600
Eh?

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:39.270
Prof. Casera!

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:40.710
Prof. Casera?

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:42.800
That's right!

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:45.200
Prof. Casera might know.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:48.730
Leon?

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:51.570
The man's name is Leon?

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.590
Do you know him, Prof. Casera?

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.850
Romeo... come with me.

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:06.100
The Leon I know has sought his father and daughter for a long time.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:10.330
He suddenly came to my door a few years ago,

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.620
...and began studying to become a doctor.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:17.290
He didn't seem to have any formal education, but he was a hard worker.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:20.780
He kept absorbing difficult subjects without complaint.

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:27.280
And now, he's...

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:42.910
Leon is in here?

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:46.520
Good. Your complexion is looking much healthier.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.590
Thank you very much, doctor.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:50.800
Keep at it.

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:53.990
That's Dr. Leon.

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:58.600
He does all he can for the sick children of the poor.

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:00.230
Dr. Leon...

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:02.060
You're looking well.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:03.270
Thank you, doctor.

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:08.080
You'll be walking without crutches in no time.

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:09.180
Really?

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:11.320
You bet.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:16.650
I finally... I finally found him, Angeletta.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:21.020
I did it, Angeletta! I did it!

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:23.290
It's a miracle!

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:29.610
Thank goodness! Really - thank goodness!

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:42.600
Nana, I'll tell you the truth one day.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:45.840
Tell me what?
A story about the moon?

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:02.430
Come this way.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:03.930
He's right over there.

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:08.380
Grampa Theo!

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:15.260
May I introduce... the best doctor in Milan... Dr. Leon!

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:27.520
Father...

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:31.370
I've finally fulfilled my dream.

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:34.880
I've been looking for you two for a long time.

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:37.300
You pigheaded...

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:40.260
Grampa!

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:41.270
Nana...

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:47.330
it's your... your...
- Father! Nana!

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:57.520
Forgive me, Leon!
- Me, too.

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:04.700
Nana...

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:06.530
It's your father.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.400
Please forgive me... Nana.

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:33.840
<i>It's good, isn't it, Angeletta?</i>

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:39.920
<i>Thank you, Romeo.</i>

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:47.660
<i>Romeo was proud to have been of service to Angeletta.</i>

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:53.300
<i>And Angeletta, too, thanked Romeo from the bottom of her heart.</i>

00:20:55.770 --> 00:21:01.550
<i>It seemed like that moment of happiness could last forever.</i>

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:09.040
<i>Yes, but how could they have guessed...</i>

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:11.800
<i>...that an unforeseen incident,</i>

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:14.860
<i>...and their day of parting, lay such a short time away?</i>

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:19.950
So, does your Angeletta up in that tower...

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.270
...know yet that she's a count's daughter?

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:24.430
Matteo, stop talking about that.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:26.810
Look at that, Rossi.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:30.070
A patrician get-together.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:32.890
Chattering about the opera, no doubt.

00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:46.580
<i>Your ladyship!</i>

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:58.940
<i>I follow the boss to Count Montovarni's mansion...</i>

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:02.510
<i>...and there I discover an undreamt-of secret!</i>

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:06.020
<i>Angeletta? A member of the Count's family?</i>

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:10.160
See you then!

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:10.160
<i>Angeletta's Secret</i>

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:10.160
Next time:

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:16.940
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:29.650
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:33.950
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:38.150
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:42.350
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:47.260
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:47.260 --> 00:22:51.160
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:51.560 --> 00:22:58.460
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:04.060
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:04.260 --> 00:23:08.260
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
